# Ponor — local environment. Copy to `.env` and fill in; `.env` is gitignored, this file is not.
#
# BOTH VARIABLES ARE OPTIONAL. With neither set the app builds, runs, logs dives and passes
# its whole test suite — DESIGN.md §1: the app runs offline from on-device SQLite, and an
# account is only needed to back up, sync a second device and contribute named sites. Set
# them when you want the cloud half; leave them out and nothing anywhere behaves differently.
# `src/cloud/supabase.ts` is where that rule is written down and defended.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ MEANS PUBLIC. READ THIS BEFORE PUTTING A KEY IN `.env`.
#
# Expo inlines every `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variable into the JavaScript bundle at build time. The
# value is not fetched, not hidden and not encrypted — it is a string literal inside an app
# anyone can download and unzip. Only put a value here that is designed to be handed out.
#
#   ✅ the ANON key ("anon public", also labelled `publishable`) — Supabase Dashboard →
#      Project Settings → API Keys. It is meant to ship inside clients; it carries no
#      privileges of its own, and Row-Level Security is what actually protects the data
#      (DESIGN.md §5: dives are readable and writable only by their owner).
#
#   ❌ the SERVICE_ROLE key (also labelled `secret`). It BYPASSES RLS COMPLETELY — every
#      dive of every user, readable and writable. Shipping it in a client hands that to
#      anyone who downloads the app. It has no business in this repository at all, which is
#      PUBLIC: not in `.env`, not in a comment, not in a commit message, not "temporarily".
#      Nothing in Ponor's client ever needs it; server-side work happens in Postgres
#      functions behind RLS (§5's RPCs), where the key stays on Supabase's side of the wire.
#      If one is ever pasted somewhere tracked, rotating it in the dashboard is the fix —
#      deleting the line is not, because git keeps it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The bundler reads this file when it starts. After editing `.env`, restart Metro (`npm
# start`) — a running bundler will not pick it up, and a production build inlines whatever
# was set when the build ran, not when the app launches.

# Your project's REST URL — Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → Data API.
# Shaped like https://<project-ref>.supabase.co (DESIGN.md §5: one project, EU/Frankfurt).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# The anon / publishable key. See the box above: this one, never the service_role key.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
